  "aboutParagraphs": [
    "Bird's Nest is a 27-hole, disc-golf-only park on 40 acres of Jefferson County open space in Arvada — one of the most-played courses in the country. Rolling pastures, tree-lined holes, and real elevation change spread across nearly 9,500 feet at par 82.",
    "Free to play and very cart friendly, with restrooms on site and a layout that flows without crossing itself. The 27 holes are one continuous loop that gives you room to air it out on the open holes and forces precision on the lined ones.",
    "It's the rare course that's both a workout and a pleasure — bring water, bring your whole bag, and bring a friend."
  ],
