  "signatureHoleDescription": "Hole 14 is Bird's Nest's only par 4 — 540 feet that breaks up the par-3 rhythm and gives the big arms their moment. A drive across the rolling pasture, then a long approach to a basket the tree line guards. It's the hole that keeps the round interesting between the marathons and the breathers.",
  "localTips": "One of the most-played courses in the country — expect a crowd on weekends. It's free, very cart friendly, and the 27 holes make it a real workout. Holes 19–27 are a little lighter on infrastructure, so pack what you need.",
